This file documents the TWO changes install.py makes (via sed) to a stock
Klipper tree; it is reference documentation, not what the installer applies:

1. src/Makefile -- compile sensor_ldc1612_ng.c alongside sensor_ldc1612.c
   (under CONFIG_WANT_LDC1612).
2. klippy/extras/bed_mesh.py -- recognize eddy-ng probes as scanning probes
   so BED_MESH_CALIBRATE METHOD=rapid_scan works (replaces the stock
   probe_eddy_current name check; the "#eddy-ng" marker is what the
   uninstaller's reverse sed keys off).

Line numbers drift with upstream Klipper; install.py patches by content.

diff --git src/Makefile src/Makefile
index cfedc56f7..422e0179e 100644
--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -20,6 +20,6 @@ src-$(CONFIG_WANT_LIS2DW) += sensor_lis2dw.c
 src-$(CONFIG_WANT_MPU9250) += sensor_mpu9250.c
 src-$(CONFIG_WANT_HX71X) += sensor_hx71x.c
 src-$(CONFIG_WANT_ADS1220) += sensor_ads1220.c
-src-$(CONFIG_WANT_LDC1612) += sensor_ldc1612.c
+src-$(CONFIG_WANT_LDC1612) += sensor_ldc1612.c sensor_ldc1612_ng.c
 src-$(CONFIG_WANT_SENSOR_ANGLE) += sensor_angle.c
 src-$(CONFIG_NEED_SENSOR_BULK) += sensor_bulk.c
diff --git klippy/extras/bed_mesh.py klippy/extras/bed_mesh.py
--- a/klippy/extras/bed_mesh.py
+++ b/klippy/extras/bed_mesh.py
@@ -869,7 +869,7 @@
         pprobe = self.printer.lookup_object("probe", None)
         if pprobe is not None:
             probe_name = pprobe.get_status(None).get("name", "")
-            can_scan = probe_name.startswith("probe_eddy_current")
+            can_scan = "eddy" in probe_name #eddy-ng
         if method == "rapid_scan" and can_scan:
             self.rapid_scan_helper.perform_rapid_scan(gcmd)
         else:
